            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was the recipe I was looking for! It was very tasty! \n\nI read the comments &amp; think I have found ways to solve the problems addressed in them. Because of the mention of the excess liquid, I had a jar of Penzy's powdered lemon zest that I used in lieu of the juice. I bet fresh would be even better. I added 1/4 cup of a can of petite diced tomatoes &amp; to counterbalance the acid, I put in 1 pinch (literally) of white sugar. It did not give any sweetness, just balanced the acid content. To also help with the liquid issue, I cooked the pasta (I used spaghetti) 2 minutes short of done, and then tossed it into the pan of sauce &amp; cooked it for the remaining 2 minutes there. \n\nThanks for the great recipe!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kate"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this all the time and it is a family favorite. I always double the recipe, and add sundried tomatoes for flavor and beautiful color.\nTwo tips - cook the shrimp BEFORE adding the asparagus to keep it crisp and bright green, and also add one ladle-full of the starchy pasta water when the shrimp and asparagus are simmering towards the end of the pasta cook time. It adds more to the \"sauce\" and fills out the dish.",
            "datePublished": "2019-07-23T18:27:52.663Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim G"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Doubled the recipe, and it was delicious. I added some lemon zest, but other than that I didn't need to change anything but maybe the amount of time to simmer down the wine. The sauce was perfect- light and delicious. Just enough heat from the red pepper flakes. I threw on a few pieces of fresh sliced tomatoes for color at the end.",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-16T23:04:30.112Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
